## B0016 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-011
   REQ-PB-011 | Show the four guiding questions and tag each deliverable with the question it answers | PROC: Each methodology template/deliverable carries one of the four questions, shown in form headers and the Playbook reader | ACC: A01: all four questions render verbatim (en) with ar translations; every seeded template has exactly one question tag
## B0024 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-001
   REQ-PB-001 | Label the methodology provenance honestly as a practical synthesis inspired by PMI/Brightline/BRM and never claim official PMI status | PROC: System displays the verbatim provenance statement in the Playbook reader, About page and generated report footers; the source-foundations table (Source / Used for) is shown read-only in the Playbook reader | ACC: A01: provenance text on reader/About/report footer matches B0004 verbatim; an automated text scan of UI strings (en+ar) and report templates finds no claim of 'official PMI standard', 'PMI certified' 
## B0032 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-022;REQ-PB-028
   REQ-PB-022 | Enforce the Gate 1 rule: no list of projects proceeds until leadership agrees on problem, baseline and material value pools | PROC: G1 approval records explicit leadership agreement on problem, baseline and material value pools; before G1 approval (End-to-End) initiatives stay Draft and cannot enter the portfolio | ACC: A08;A02: G1 approval without the three agreement confirmations is rejected; pre-G1, adding an initiative to the portfolio returns 409
   REQ-PB-028 | Record value pools quantified by driver with upside and downside | PROC: Users quantify value pools by driver; material pools are flagged for G1 agreement; unquantified pools are labelled explicitly | ACC: A01: a value pool without quantification is shown as 'unquantified', not zero; material pools appear in the G1 pack
## B0037 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-030
   REQ-PB-030 | Capture the transformation thesis in its four-part causal sentence | PROC: Charter includes a structured thesis; the system renders 'If we change ..., then ... will improve, which will create ..., because ...' | ACC: A01: thesis with any of the four parts empty is flagged incomplete; rendered sentence matches the source structure
## B0051 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-036
   REQ-PB-036 | Apply the good outcome test to every outcome | PROC: Each outcome shows the five criteria; system checks measurable (KPI linked), owned (owner set) and flags statements that are only 'launch', 'implement' or 'deliver' | ACC: A01: an outcome worded 'Launch new app' with no KPI fails the test with reasons; G2 readiness lists failing outcomes
## B0059 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-040
   REQ-PB-040 | Keep the TOM distinct from the project portfolio | PROC: TOM records describe the future operating state; initiatives are a separate entity linked as vehicles to TOM gaps; G3 evidence can't be satisfied by initiatives | ACC: A01: attaching an initiative as G3 TOM evidence is rejected; an initiative links to one or more TOM gaps
## B0088 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-058
   REQ-PB-058 | Prevent double counting: each benefit has a unique owner, baseline, formula and financial-statement or non-financial KPI link | PROC: System rejects a benefit without a single owner, baseline, formula and a financial statement line or agreed non-financial KPI; initiatives link to canonical benefits via allocations, parent/child relationships and shared-benefit groups; portfolio totals sum ca | ACC: A10: a benefit with two owners is rejected; a 10 million SAR benefit shared by two initiatives appears once (10 million SAR) in the portfolio total
## B0102 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-068
   REQ-PB-068 | Enforce the governance rule: escalate decisions, not status | PROC: An executive agenda item cannot be published unless it states all five elements | ACC: A09: publishing an agenda item missing 'Impact of delay' is rejected by the API
## B0116 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-073
   REQ-PB-073 | Apply the people-centered principle: record impacted-team involvement in design and champion constraints | PROC: Design workshops and decisions record which impacted teams participated; champions can raise constraints that link to design decisions | ACC: A01;A11: a champion's constraint links to a T04 decision and is visible on that decision
## B0124 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-077
   REQ-PB-077 | Label the Realize phase as aligned with PMI BRM logic without claiming PMI standard status | PROC: The Realize phase guidance shows the note that it aligns with PMI Benefits Realization Management logic | ACC: A01: Realize guidance shows 'aligns with PMI Benefits Realization Management logic' and no 'certified'/'official' wording
## B0131 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-082
   REQ-PB-082 | Apply the escalation principle: a blocker red for multiple cycles requires a named decision, owner and deadline | PROC: When a blocker stays Red across the configured number of cycles, the system requires/creates a T16 executive ask with decision, owner and deadline, without duplicating an existing open ask | ACC: A09;A13: a blocker Red in 2 consecutive cycles (N=2) produces exactly one open T16 ask; re-running the job creates no duplicate
## B0156 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-001
   REQ-PB-001 | Label the methodology provenance honestly as a practical synthesis inspired by PMI/Brightline/BRM and never claim official PMI status | PROC: System displays the verbatim provenance statement in the Playbook reader, About page and generated report footers; the source-foundations table (Source / Used for) is shown read-only in the Playbook reader | ACC: A01: provenance text on reader/About/report footer matches B0004 verbatim; an automated text scan of UI strings (en+ar) and report templates finds no claim of 'official PMI standard', 'PMI certified' 
## B0008 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-003;REQ-PB-005
   REQ-PB-003 | Offer the two source usage modes End-to-End and Modular when creating or entering a transformation | PROC: User creating a transformation selects a mode; the form shows the source 'When to use' and 'How' guidance for each mode; Modular requires an entry phase | ACC: A01;A03: API accepts mode End-to-End or Modular only; Modular without entry phase is rejected with a validation error; guidance text shows 'Run Phases 1-6 sequentially...' and 'Enter at the relevant p
   REQ-PB-005 | Support Modular entry at a chosen phase or as a standalone TOM, business case or benefits register and flag missing links to outcomes and benefits | PROC: User enters at the relevant phase, completes the minimum mandatory templates, and reconnects to outcomes and benefits; the system lists missing upstream links and never marks earlier gates approved without recorded evidence | ACC: A03: a transformation entering at Design with no baseline and no outcome links shows both as missing and G3 submission is rejected by the API until they are supplied or an authorized waiver exists
## B0011 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-006
   REQ-PB-006 | Apply 'Outcome before activity': initiatives cannot be submitted for prioritization without a linked measurable outcome | PROC: When an initiative is submitted to the prioritization scorecard or to G4 evidence, the system checks for at least one linked outcome with a KPI | ACC: A01: submitting an initiative with no outcome/KPI link returns a validation error naming 'Outcome before activity'; the same initiative with a link is accepted
## B0012 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-007
   REQ-PB-007 | Apply 'Current state before solution': require a diagnostic covering economics, customer, operations, capability and technology before initiatives are prescribed | PROC: In End-to-End mode, initiatives created before the G1 diagnostic is approved stay in Draft; the diagnostic readiness shows which of the diagnosed areas are missing | ACC: A01;A02: before G1 approval an initiative cannot leave Draft (API 409); readiness lists missing diagnostic dimensions
## B0013 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-008
   REQ-PB-008 | Apply 'Operating model before execution': decision rights, ownership and cross-functional ways of working are explicit before execution | PROC: Execution-phase readiness (Transform) checks that the charter's decision rights are filled, T11 has at least the seeded decisions with an Approve role, and T12 has an accountable role per deliverable | ACC: A01: readiness for Transform shows 'not ready' when T11 or charter decision rights are empty and 'ready' once they are completed
## B0014 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-009
   REQ-PB-009 | Apply 'Benefits before closure': an initiative is complete only when value is realized and sustained, not when delivered | PROC: Initiatives carry separate delivery, value-realization and sustainment statuses; closure requires validated benefits and sustainment owner or a documented transition decision | ACC: A11: an initiative with delivery=Complete and no validated benefit cannot be closed (API 409); UI shows 'Delivered — value validation pending'
## B0015 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-010
   REQ-PB-010 | Apply 'One source of truth': keep the charter, roadmap, initiative portfolio and benefits register linked as canonical records | PROC: Charter, roadmap, portfolio and benefits register reference the same canonical records (no copies); editing an initiative updates its roadmap and benefits views | ACC: A01: renaming an initiative changes it in roadmap, scorecard and benefits register views in one update; no duplicate initiative rows exist in the database
## B0063 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-042
   REQ-PB-042 | Support the TOM canvas workshop and convert unresolved items into design decisions with owners | PROC: Facilitator publishes an agenda and runs a workshop session with business owners, capturing contributions per dimension; each unresolved item is converted in one action into a T04 design decision with owner (source) or an owned action (extension) | ACC: A01: converting an unresolved item creates a T04 row linked to the workshop with owner set; an item without an owner cannot be converted; converting an item to an action creates an owned action linked
## B0084 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-013;REQ-PB-054;REQ-PB-055
   REQ-PB-013 | Restrict Finance / Value Office validation of baseline, benefit logic and value realization to the Finance role | PROC: Only users holding FIN on the transformation can mark a baseline, benefit formula or realized value as validated; others can submit for validation | ACC: A10;A12: a Business Owner calling the validate endpoint receives 403; a Finance user succeeds and the audit event records validator identity
   REQ-PB-054 | Support a transformation-level business case with lighter linked initiative cases | PROC: Initiative cases are lighter forms linked to the transformation case; roll-up references, not copies | ACC: A01;A10: an initiative case links to one transformation case; editing the initiative case changes the transformation roll-up without duplicating benefits
   REQ-PB-055 | Require Finance validation of baseline and benefit logic early, before G4, not after delivery | PROC: A business case cannot be submitted as G4 evidence until Finance has validated its baseline and benefit formulas | ACC: A08;A10: G4 submission with a business case whose benefit formula is unvalidated is rejected listing 'Finance validation'
## B0105 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-069
   REQ-PB-069 | Manage adoption as an outcome with measurable leading indicators, separate from delivery | PROC: Adoption has its own outcome, KPIs and status distinct from initiative delivery status; adoption KPIs use trajectories, and a gap beyond threshold creates one intervention with owner | ACC: A11: an initiative with delivery Complete and adoption below trajectory shows adoption at risk and triggers an intervention; an adoption actual below trajectory creates exactly one intervention
## B0161 REQUIREMENT REQ-PB-002;REQ-PB-060;REQ-PB-086;REQ-PB-091
   REQ-PB-002 | Mark custom extensions of the playbook distinctly from PMI/Brightline-derived foundations | PROC: Each seeded methodology element (phases, TOM dimensions, gates, templates, scoring model, cadence, launch plan, health check, roaming example, traceability chain) carries a provenance attribute 'custom extension (playbook v1.0)' shown as a badge in the Playboo | ACC: A01: every seeded element listed in B0158-B0162 returns provenance=custom-extension from the API and renders the badge in en and ar; no such element is labelled as a PMI standard
   REQ-PB-060 | Seed the five transformation operating system layers with cadence, purpose, participants and outputs | PROC: Seed Executive SteerCo (Monthly), Transformation Review (Bi-weekly), Workstream Review (Weekly), Rapid Response / Sprint (Daily / 2-3x week), Value Review (Monthly) as forums with recurrence and participants | ACC: A01: the five layers are seeded with cadence text verbatim; a forum meeting series generates meetings on the configured recurrence
   REQ-PB-086 | Seed the 90-day launch plan as scheduled tasks relative to a start date | PROC: On request, the system generates tasks for each window's actions and required outputs, dated from the chosen start date, with owners and links to the output records | ACC: A16: with start date 2026-10-01 the Days 31-60 tasks fall between 2026-11-01 and 2026-11-30; all actions of B0134 appear
   REQ-PB-091 | Implement the 25-question Transformation Health Check with score and top 3 actions | PROC: Assessor answers all 25 questions; score out of 25 is calculated; three top actions are required; reassessments tracked | ACC: A16: all 25 questions render verbatim; an assessment with an unanswered question is labelled incomplete and shows no band; submission without three actions is rejected
